    {
      "heading": "Two jumps change the gold chase",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "AquaUrsa Research has broken into the provisional gold places with 38.97, reaching 14th after an observed jump from 30.21. A second late move put the entry listed as “speed, my mom is kinda homless”, whose roster contains mellamoa, 16th at 38.22. The two advances lift contenders out of the chasing pack while the public gold cutoff rises from 37.18 to 37.98. Both now sit inside the 18 gold places; those positions remain provisional."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Improving is no guarantee of holding ground",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-lord-han-solo-identity-0",
        "person-daniel-franzen-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Lord Han Solo improved from 36.98 to 37.07 in an overnight score event, yet closes this edition 22nd. Daniel Franzen’s observed rise from 35.86 to 36.86 leaves him 24th. Their gains did not keep pace with the medal line: the gap is now nearly a point for Lord Han Solo and just over a point for Franzen. These are current board results, separate from any earlier qualifying milestone prizes."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The leaders keep their distance",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-dries-smit-identity-0",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs remains first at 68.91 ahead of Yi-Chia Chen at 67.49, with both scores unchanged from the overnight baseline. Their advantage over third-place mtg, on 45, remains substantial. NVARC3 holds fourth ahead of the last dance in fifth; Son & Mark & Ronen remains seventh. None of those teams changed score in the edition comparison. The new Walking Foundry illustration returns to this leading group as a sporting metaphor; its fanciful GPU equipment describes no team’s actual hardware."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The next tier also moves",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Julian Hermes reached 34.95 in an observed climb from 78th to 35th. Later, Matija L & Zhongwei W & Fususu reached 35.62 in an observed move from 353rd to 31st. Those event ranks describe the board when each change was recorded, rather than guaranteed closing positions. The medal stories above show how quickly another submission can change that picture."
    }
